### Details
I have added NumberConvert.js in libs directory. It exposes two methods. toLocalPhone(locale, number) and fromLocalPhone(locale, number). I have also added phoneCountryCode key in both en and es-ES.
1. toLocalPhone(locale, number)  takes two arguments i.e. locale eg. es-ES and number for example +17474747474. It trims the country code from the phone number depending upon the locale given. It fetches the respective country codes from the /languages/translations. 
2. fromLocalPhone(locale, number)  takes two arguments i.e. locale eg. es-ES and number for example +17474747474. It adds the country code from the phone number depending upon the locale given ( if not already added ). It fetches the respective country codes from the /languages/translations as well.
3. I have made use of loadash to perform all the utility operations.
4. I have also trimmed any spaces if given at start or end of the number. 

### Fixed Issues
Fixes https://github.com/Expensify/Expensify.cash/issues/2089

